.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-config-set 1  "tapectl-config-set " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-config\-set \- Set one key in config.toml, keeping its comments and layout
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl config set\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIKEY\fR> <\fIVALUE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set one key in config.toml, keeping its comments and layout
.PP
KEY is a dotted path as `config check` prints it: `defaults.slice_size`, `host_check.max_load_per_cpu`. An entry of a list of tables is selected by its name or its position from 0: `collections[movies].unit_depth`, `backends.lto[0].enospc_buffer`. A missing table is created.
.PP
VALUE is tried as a TOML number, boolean or array first, and as a string when that does not load; quote it as TOML (`\*(Aq"3"\*(Aq`) to force a string. The edited file is checked as every command loads it before it is written: an unknown key or a bad value is refused by name and the file is left exactly as it was. The file is replaced atomically.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
No live progress on stderr. Long operations (stage create, volume write/resume/verify/read\-slices, restore) still write their session log under <home>/logs/
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, stage reports. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home.
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, stage\-reports, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIKEY\fR>
The key, e.g. defaults.slice_size
.TP
<\fIVALUE\fR>
The value, e.g. 2G
